{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793739647,"nonce":"rfu7nnTfwu82Scj9qxKOe6lm4j8=","title":"An adaptive load path returns frames interpolated between solved steps","message":"`fem.solve(tau=jno.solve.adaptive(...))` solves on the steps the controller chooses and resamples the trajectory linearly onto the domain's declared tau grid. When the controller takes fewer steps than the grid has levels, most returned frames are blends of two solutions, not solutions. Nothing in the result says which frames were solved.\n\nSeen on a phase-field fracture march: 8 solved steps returned as 24 frames, so the damage field appears to fade in between steps where it really jumps.\n\nQuestion: return the solved states (with `fem.tau_schedule`) instead, or mark the interpolated frames, or warn when the grid is finer than the schedule.","files":null}]}